"007:001 And it came to pass in the days of Achaz the son of Joatham, the son of Ozias, king of Juda, there came up Rasim king of Aram, and Phakee son of Romelias, king of Israel, against Jerusalem to war against it, but they could not take it.",
"007:002 And a message was brought to the house of David, saying, Aram has conspired with Ephraim. And his soul was amazed, and the soul of his people, as in a wood a tree is moved by the wind.",
"007:003 And the Lord said to Esaias, Go forth to meet Achaz, you, and your son Jasub who is left, to the pool of the upper way of the fuller's field.",
"007:004 And you shall say to him, Take care to be quiet, and fear not, neither let your soul be disheartened because of these two smoking firebrands: for when my fierce anger is over, I will heal again.",
"007:005 And as for the son of Aram, and the son of Romelias, forasmuch as they have devised an evil counsel, saying,",
"007:006 We will go up against Judea, and having conferred with them we will turn them away to our side, and we will make the son of Tabeel king of it;",
"007:007 thus says the Lord of hosts, This counsel shall not abide, nor come to pass.",
"007:008 But the head of Aram is Damascus, and the head of Damascus, Rasim; and yet within sixty and five years the kingdom of Ephraim shall cease from being a people.",
"007:009 And the head of Ephraim is Somoron, and the head of Somoron the son of Romelias: but if you believe not, neither will you at all understand.",
"007:010 And the Lord again spoke to Achaz, saying,",
"007:011 Ask for yourself a sign of the Lord your God, in the depth or in the height.",
"007:012 And Achaz said, I will not ask, neither will I tempt the Lord.",
"007:013 And he said, Hear you now, O house of David; is it a little thing for you to contend with men? and how do you contend against the Lord?",
"007:014 Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; behold, a virgin shall conceive in the womb, and shall bring forth a son, and you shall call his name Emmanuel.",
"007:015 Butter and honey shall he eat, before he knows either to prefer evil or choose the good.",
"007:016 For before the child shall know good or evil, he refuses evil, to choose the good; and the land shall be forsaken which you are afraid of because of the two kings.",
"007:017 But God shall bring upon you, and upon your people, and upon the house of your father, days which have never come, from the day that Ephraim took away from Juda the king of the Assyrians.",
"007:018 And it shall come to pass in that day that the Lord shall hiss for the flies, which insect shall rule over a part of the river of Egypt, and for the bee which is in the land of the Assyrians.",
"007:019 And they all shall enter into the clefts of the land, and into the holes of the rocks, and into the caves, and into every ravine.",
"007:020 In that day the Lord shall shave with the hired razor of the king of Assyria beyond the river the head, and the hairs of the feet, and will remove the beard.",
"007:021 And it shall come to pass in that day, that a man shall rear a heifer, and two sheep.",
"007:022 And it shall come to pass from their drinking an abundance of milk, that every one that is left on the land shall eat butter and honey.",
"007:023 And it shall come to pass in that day, for every place where there shall be a thousand vines at a thousand shekels, they shall become barren land and thorns.",
"007:024 Men shall enter there with arrow and bow; for all the land shall be barren ground and thorns.",
"007:025 And every mountain shall be certainly ploughed: there shall no fear come there: for there shall be from amongst the barren ground and thorns that whereon cattle shall feed and oxen shall tread."
